Day 37: Preparing the Heart | Thursday of the Fifth Week of Lent (Lent Devotional)

📌 YouTube Description
A humble heart.
An open heart.
A heart that is ready.

Welcome to Day 37 of our Lent journey.
As Lent draws near its climax, today’s reflection invites you into a posture of quiet openness — the kind of heart that can receive the mystery, beauty, and depth of Holy Week. God is not asking for perfection. He is asking for willingness. A softened heart becomes the soil where grace takes root.

This spoken‑word devotional reminds you that a broken and contrite heart is not rejected by God — it is welcomed, held, and transformed. These final days of Lent invite you to slow down, to soften, and to let God prepare you for what is coming.

In today’s reflection, you’ll hear:

Why a humble heart prepares you for the mystery of the Passion

How openness, not perfection, draws you closer to God

Why Lent invites you to be shaped, moved, and changed

A prayer to ready your heart for Holy Week

A simple daily activity: whispering, “Lord, prepare my heart.”

